<title>NORWAY: NORDIC SKIING - DAEHLIE WINS 10-KM, MYLLYLA THIRD.</title>
<headline>NORDIC SKIING - DAEHLIE WINS 10-KM, MYLLYLA THIRD.</headline>
<dateline>TRONDHEIM, Norway 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bjorn Daehlie of Norway won the 10-km, classical-style cross-country race at the Nordic skiing world championships on Monday in a provisional time of 23 minutes 41.80 seconds.</p>
<p>Alexei Prokurorov of Russia was second, 27.9 seconds behind, and Mika Myllyla of Finland was third a further 4.5 seconds back, according to provisional results.</p>
